te report.json, then verify pytest. That's about: 3 read calls + 1 notes call + 1 report write + 1 verify + finish = 7. Tight but feasible. Actually I can combine: read 40-44 and 45-49 in one response? That would be ~10 pages ≈ 40k chars in next request — too much.\n\nAlternatively I could reduce: do read_pdf 40-45 (6 pages, ~25k) then 46-52 (7 pages, ~28k)? Risky.\n\nLet me be careful: what content do I actually still need? The five topics: overview (p1-2), reasoning (Self Consistency, ToT — probably p12-16), tool_use (Toolformer, ToolBench — p20-24), multi_agent (CAMEL p37, Generative Agents evaluators — p39-41?), outlook (Table 4, conclusion — near p48-52). So remaining pages 40-52 needed for: Generative Agents evaluators (maybe p40), outlook (Table 4, conclusion p48-52).\n\nBut the task requires reading all 52 pages and all must enter model requests. The state shows pages 1-39 already exposed. So I need 40-52 read for real (command_result recorded). I must comply: read 40-52 via read_pdf.\n\nI don't remember details from pages 1-39 well (I have no notes). I need quotes for evidence. I'll need to recall specific pages via get_evidence for key facts. That costs calls too.\n\nHmm, evidence_catalog has 51 entries; pages 1-39 exposed. To write evidence quotes I need exact text. I can recall via get_evidence for specific pages (e.g., page 1 for categories, page ~13 for self-consistency, page ~21 for Toolformer, page 37 for CAMEL, page 39 Generative Agents). But get_evidence pins content in next request consuming budget.\n\nPlan with 10 calls:\n1. read_pdf 40-45 (6 pages). (~26k chars)\n2. read_pdf 46-52 (7 pages) — might be ~30k? Pages 46-52 include references start at 52. Risky but let's try; maybe 5 pages 46-50 then 51-52.\n\nActually, maybe I can combine a read_pdf call with get_evidence recalls in the same response — but total next-request size must be ≤32k, so no.\n\nLet me think about efficiency: I could skip get_evidence and instead in the same response as writ